  "question": "Background / Context\nThe project involves utilizing the PKDD'99 Financial dataset, which contains information on 606 successful loans and 76 unsuccessful loans, along with associated account and transaction details. The dataset aims to assist in understanding and predicting loan outcomes based on historical financial data at the starting point of the loan.\n\n Objectives\nThe primary objective is to develop a system capable of predicting the outcome of a loan (successful or unsuccessful) at the time of loan initiation. This predictive capability will help financial institutions assess risks and make informed lending decisions.\n\n Stakeholders & Users\n- Financial Analysts: Use the system to analyze loan data and predict outcomes.\n- Loan Officers: Aid in decision-making for approving or rejecting loan applications.\n- Data Scientists & Engineers: Implement and maintain prediction models and system infrastructure.\n\n Functional Descriptions\n1. Data Management:\n   - Store and manage account, client, and transaction information.\n   - Track loan details, including amount, duration, and status.\n\n2. Predictive Modeling:\n   - Analyze historical loan data to train predictive models.\n   - Provide predictions on loan status (A: successful, B: unsuccessful) at initiation.\n\n3. User Interface:\n   - Enable users to input loan parameters and receive predictions.\n   - Display detailed account and transaction history for analysis.\n\n4. Reporting:\n   - Generate reports on prediction accuracy and loan performance.\n   - Facilitate trend analysis and risk assessment.\n\n5. Integration:\n   - Seamlessly integrate with existing financial management systems.\n\n Non-Functional Descriptions\n- Performance: The system should provide predictions quickly (within seconds) to support real-time decision-making.\n- Scalability: Capable of handling a large volume of loans and transactions efficiently.\n- Security: Ensure data privacy and protection, especially sensitive financial and personal information.\n- Reliability: Provide consistent and reliable predictions with minimal downtime.\n- Usability: Intuitive interface for users with varying technical expertise.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0107\nCREATE TABLE `district` (\n  `district_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `district_name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`district_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `client` (\n  `client_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `district_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `birth_number` char(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `gender` char(1) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `client_name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`client_id`),\n  KEY `client_ibfk_1` (`district_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `client_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`district_id`) REFERENCES `district` (`district_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `account` (\n  `account_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `district_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `frequency` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `date_opened` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`account_id`),\n  KEY `account_ibfk_1` (`district_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `account_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`district_id`) REFERENCES `district` (`district_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `disposition` (\n  `disp_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `client_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `account_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `type` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`disp_id`),\n  KEY `disposition_ibfk_1` (`client_id`),\n  KEY `disposition_ibfk_2` (`account_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `disposition_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`client_id`) REFERENCES `client` (`client_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `disposition_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`account_id`) REFERENCES `account` (`account_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `loan` (\n  `loan_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `account_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `date_issued` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `amount` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `duration_months` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `payments` decimal(10,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `status` char(1) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`loan_id`),\n  KEY `loan_ibfk_1` (`account_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `loan_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`account_id`) REFERENCES `account` (`account_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `transaction` (\n  `transaction_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `account_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `transaction_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `transaction_type` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `operation` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `amount` decimal(10,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `balance` decimal(10,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `k_symbol` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `bank` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `account` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`transaction_id`),\n  KEY `transaction_ibfk_1` (`account_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `transaction_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`account_id`) REFERENCES `account` (`account_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
